// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Radmin DLL Sideloading From User AppData
// Sigma ID: 7b9139bc-caba-464b-a932-dc7e1dca6eb9
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: brandolphj
// Date: 2026-10-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: T1574.001
// Description: Detects the Radmin executable FamItrfc.exe loading BlkScrDl.dll from a user's local AppData
//   Radmin directory, as observed in a reported supply-chain compromise.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/investigating-ephemeral-supply-chain-tampering
//   - https://www.manageengine.com/threat-analysis-lab/aomei-backupper-supply-chain-compromise.html
//   - https://labs.cloudsecurityalliance.org/research/csa-research-note-aomei-backupper-update-server-tampering-20/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/0e1fa4c6be0be78a310ec310cb11f874488e5520/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_win_radmin_dll_sideloading.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\AppData\\Local\\Radmin\\FamItrfc.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\AppData\\Local\\Radmin\\BlkScrDl.dll"
